{"hash":"2ec2f8dd511e99ed","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":83.765,"said":"This is Shivalaya, the great stepped tank. Look down the flights of stone to the green water far below. One night, the Purana says, while the house slept, Sudeha killed her sister’s son, and threw his body into this very lake, the lake where Ghushma let her lingas go each day. In the morning the house woke to grief. Only Ghushma did not stop her worship. ‘He who gave me this child,’ she said, ‘will protect him too.’ She made her hundred and one lingas, worshipped them, and came down here to let them go into the water. And as she turned back, there on the bank stood her son, alive. Then Shiva himself appeared in all his radiance, his trident raised against Sudeha. But Ghushma fell at his feet and begged him to spare her sister. Pleased by a heart that could forgive even this, Shiva offered her a boon. She asked him to stay here for ever, for the good of the world. He agreed. He became Ghushmeshwara, the Lord of Ghushma, and this lake took the name Shivalaya, the home of Shiva. Now walk back with me to the temple, to the place where he stayed.\n\nDid you know? The short Jyotirlinga Stotram remembers this lake: it names the twelfth Jyotirlinga ‘Ghushmesham cha Shivalaye’, Ghushmesha at Shivalaya.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1057},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1073,"end":1210}],"words":[[0.098,0.264,0,4],[0.374,0.096,5,7],[0.483,0.613,8,17],[1.24,0.108,19,22],[1.36,0.349,23,28],[1.721,0.397,29,36],[2.129,0.445,37,41],[3.462,0.216,43,47],[3.69,0.276,48,52],[3.978,0.084,53,56],[4.074,0.421,57,64],[4.507,0.108,65,67],[4.627,0.397,68,73],[5.036,0.108,74,76],[5.156,0.096,77,80],[5.264,0.373,81,86],[5.649,0.325,87,92],[5.986,0.276,93,96],[6.274,0.397,97,102],[7.584,0.312,104,107],[7.909,0.373,108,113],[8.51,0.096,115,118],[8.618,0.457,119,125],[9.087,0.433,126,130],[9.784,0.276,132,137],[10.072,0.084,138,141],[10.168,0.337,142,147],[10.517,0.445,148,153],[11.142,0.